    loading=&quot;lazy&quot;
    decoding=&quot;async&quot;&gt;
  
  
  
  &lt;figcaption&gt;Dr. Maryna Kuzmenko with Marc Jones from Antobot.&lt;/figcaption&gt;
  
&lt;/figure&gt;


&lt;div class=&quot;photo-grid photo-grid--portrait&quot;&gt;
  
&lt;figure class=&quot;page-figure&quot;&gt;
  &lt;img
    src=&quot;/assets/img/events/2026-10-08-Fruit-Attraction/humanoid-robot-fruit-attraction-2026-640.webp&quot;
    srcset=&quot;/assets/img/events/2026-10-08-Fruit-Attraction/humanoid-robot-fruit-attraction-2026-480.webp 480w, /assets/img/events/2026-10-08-Fruit-Attraction/humanoid-robot-fruit-attraction-2026-640.webp 640w&quot;
    sizes=&quot;(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 330px&quot;
    width=&quot;640&quot;
    height=&quot;1422&quot;
    alt=&quot;A white humanoid robot on a wheeled base in an exhibition aisle, beside crates of produce.&quot;
    loading=&quot;lazy&quot;
    decoding=&quot;async&quot;&gt;
  
  
  
  &lt;figcaption&gt;A humanoid robot on the show floor.&lt;/figcaption&gt;
  
&lt;/figure&gt;

  
&lt;figure class=&quot;page-figure&quot;&gt;
  &lt;img
    src=&quot;/assets/img/events/2026-10-08-Fruit-Attraction/crate-carrying-robot-fruit-attraction-2026-640.webp&quot;
    srcset=&quot;/assets/img/events/2026-10-08-Fruit-Attraction/crate-carrying-robot-fruit-attraction-2026-480.webp 480w, /assets/img/events/2026-10-08-Fruit-Attraction/crate-carrying-robot-fruit-attraction-2026-640.webp 640w&quot;
    sizes=&quot;(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 330px&quot;
    width=&quot;640&quot;
    height=&quot;1422&quot;
    alt=&quot;A compact wheeled robot with a red frame carrying a blue produce crate, on a stand.&quot;
    loading=&quot;lazy&quot;
    decoding=&quot;async&quot;&gt;
  
  
  
  &lt;figcaption&gt;A wheeled robot built to carry produce crates.&lt;/figcaption&gt;
  
&lt;/figure&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;num&quot;&gt;5.&lt;/span&gt; RFID, if you&#39;re serious about traceability&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;RFID is an interesting direction if you&#39;re serious about traceability. Tracking produce from farm to supermarket shelf solves lots of compliance issues. One thing to remember: overlapping. I studied it for a Petiole Pro case study (it&#39;s a different story on another day 👍🏼).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Choosing an RFID provider is a responsible decision, like a marriage :) Why? Because once their RFID is in, they have kind of a monopoly for you, and everything next has to align with them.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;So choose someone who doesn&#39;t just want your money but feels like a team member 🤝&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;There were also drones for spraying, software of all colours and sizes + lots of smaller physical AI projects for both in-field phenotyping and post harvest.&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;figure class=&quot;page-figure page-figure--portrait&quot;&gt;
  &lt;img
    src=&quot;/assets/img/events/2026-10-08-Fruit-Attraction/robot-arm-post-harvest-fruit-attraction-2026-640.webp&quot;
