  <entry>
    <title>World Agri-Tech London 2026, Day 2: AI in Agriculture, Excitement and a Healthy Alarm</title>
    <link href="https://marynakuzmenko.com/insights/world-agri-tech-london-2026-day-2/" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <id>https://marynakuzmenko.com/insights/world-agri-tech-london-2026-day-2/</id>
    <published>2026-09-29T00:00:00.000Z</published>
    <updated>2026-10-10T14:26:45.000Z</updated>
    <summary>Day 2 of the World Agri-Tech Innovation Summit was about AI in agriculture: 400 crop-robotics startups, quick wins in the packhouse, the data-ownership question, and why the risks of AI call for awareness, not panic.</summary>
    <category term="worldagritech"/>
    <category term="agritech"/>
    <category term="AIinAgriculture"/>
    <content type="html" xml:base="https://marynakuzmenko.com/insights/world-agri-tech-london-2026-day-2/">

&lt;p class=&quot;post-intro&quot;&gt;World Agri-Tech Party – Day 2.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We spoke a lot about AI in Agriculture, and I have such dual feelings about it right now. Two days in London only amplified them.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;The first feeling: excitement&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The first feeling is obvious: excitement. AI is already bringing a lot of positive change to farming. This was confirmed at the expert panel on autonomous and precision farming and at a 40-minute workshop on Agentic AI in Agriculture.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The headliner of both was Dr Elliott Grant, who knows the subject not from the news, but from the depth &amp;amp; inside.&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;figure class=&quot;page-figure&quot;&gt;
  &lt;img
    src=&quot;/assets/img/events/2026-09-23-WATIS-2/maryna-kuzmenko-elliott-grant-cambridge-world-agri-tech-2026-1200.webp&quot;
    srcset=&quot;/assets/img/events/2026-09-23-WATIS-2/maryna-kuzmenko-elliott-grant-cambridge-world-agri-tech-2026-480.webp 480w, /assets/img/events/2026-09-23-WATIS-2/maryna-kuzmenko-elliott-grant-cambridge-world-agri-tech-2026-1200.webp 1200w&quot;
