    decoding=&quot;async&quot;&gt;
  
  
  
  &lt;figcaption&gt;Dr. Maryna Kuzmenko with Dr Elliott Grant, Institute for Manufacturing, University of Cambridge.&lt;/figcaption&gt;
  
&lt;/figure&gt;


&lt;p&gt;A few insightful things:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;num&quot;&gt;1.&lt;/span&gt; A very dynamic market&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Around 400 ag automation startups are on the latest crop robotics landscape.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;num&quot;&gt;2.&lt;/span&gt; The drivers are real&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I hear them on my own Zoom calls with farmers, especially in the Global South: labour shortages, rising input costs, pressure on pesticides.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;num&quot;&gt;3.&lt;/span&gt; Quick AI wins are simple&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A robot that just moves fruit around a packhouse frees the best pickers to keep picking.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;photo-grid&quot;&gt;
  
&lt;figure class=&quot;page-figure&quot;&gt;
  &lt;img
    src=&quot;/assets/img/events/2026-09-23-WATIS-2/maryna-kuzmenko-rob-lind-syngenta-spot-robot-world-agri-tech-2026-1200.webp&quot;
