  <entry>
    <title>World Agri-Tech London 2026, Day 1: Invention Isn&#39;t the Problem. Adoption Is.</title>
    <link href="https://marynakuzmenko.com/insights/world-agri-tech-london-2026-day-1/" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <id>https://marynakuzmenko.com/insights/world-agri-tech-london-2026-day-1/</id>
    <published>2026-09-28T00:00:00.000Z</published>
    <updated>2026-10-10T14:26:45.000Z</updated>
    <summary>Field notes from Day 1 of the World Agri-Tech Innovation Summit in London: precision-bred crops, a crowded biostimulant market, input dependency, offline resilience, and why farmers want insight, not more data.</summary>
    <category term="worldagritech"/>
    <category term="agritech"/>
    <content type="html" xml:base="https://marynakuzmenko.com/insights/world-agri-tech-london-2026-day-1/">

&lt;p class=&quot;post-intro&quot;&gt;World Agri-Tech Summit London, Day 1. But I prefer to call it the World Agri-Tech Party 🤩&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;LinkedIn generously gives me 3,000 characters to describe a day worth a book at least. Or even two :)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The second book would definitely be about the beautiful view of Canary Wharf from the window. But the first big, thick book, printed on budget paper, would be about what is actually slowing agritech down.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It&#39;s definitely not &lt;em&gt;only&lt;/em&gt; about biology. We&#39;re seeing interesting progress there, but there is also the people-money-government side. And this is where the attention goes.&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;figure class=&quot;page-figure&quot;&gt;
  &lt;img
    src=&quot;/assets/img/events/2026-09-28-WATIS/maryna-kuzmenko-jane-byrne-world-agri-tech-london-2026-1200.webp&quot;
    srcset=&quot;/assets/img/events/2026-09-28-WATIS/maryna-kuzmenko-jane-byrne-world-agri-tech-london-2026-480.webp 480w, /assets/img/events/2026-09-28-WATIS/maryna-kuzmenko-jane-byrne-world-agri-tech-london-2026-1200.webp 1200w&quot;
    sizes=&quot;(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 860px&quot;
    width=&quot;1200&quot;
    height=&quot;900&quot;
    alt=&quot;Dr. Maryna Kuzmenko and Jane Byrne, both wearing green lanyards, in a selfie beside a World Agri-Tech banner in a hotel lobby.&quot;
    loading=&quot;lazy&quot;
    decoding=&quot;async&quot;&gt;
  
  
  
  &lt;figcaption&gt;Dr. Maryna Kuzmenko with Jane Byrne, Conference Producer of World Agri-Tech London.&lt;/figcaption&gt;
  
&lt;/figure&gt;


&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;num&quot;&gt;1.&lt;/span&gt; Biologicals and gene editing dominated the startup conversation&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In England, Defra has now confirmed five crops as precision bred, the first step to market:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
  &lt;li&gt;high-lipid barley,&lt;/li&gt;
  &lt;li&gt;low-asparagine wheat,&lt;/li&gt;
  &lt;li&gt;disease-resistant Maris Piper potato,&lt;/li&gt;
  &lt;li&gt;everbearing strawberries, and&lt;/li&gt;
  &lt;li&gt;the high-vitamin D &quot;Sunshine&quot; tomato.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Meanwhile, on approvals: EU approval for a biocontrol can take 10–12 years, against about 3 in the US and 2 in Brazil. Hence, European startups sell out or launch elsewhere.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;photo-grid&quot;&gt;
  
&lt;figure class=&quot;page-figure&quot;&gt;
  &lt;img
    src=&quot;/assets/img/events/2026-09-28-WATIS/stephen-morgan-ministerial-address-world-agri-tech-london-2026-1200.webp&quot;
    srcset=&quot;/assets/img/events/2026-09-28-WATIS/stephen-morgan-ministerial-address-world-agri-tech-london-2026-480.webp 480w, /assets/img/events/2026-09-28-WATIS/stephen-morgan-ministerial-address-world-agri-tech-london-2026-1200.webp 1200w&quot;
    sizes=&quot;(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 410px&quot;
    width=&quot;1200&quot;
    height=&quot;675&quot;
    alt=&quot;Stephen Morgan MP speaking from a lectern on the summit stage, with a large screen behind him reading Ministerial Address, Stephen Morgan MP, Department for Environment, Food and Rural Affairs.&quot;
    loading=&quot;lazy&quot;
    decoding=&quot;async&quot;&gt;
  
  
  
  &lt;figcaption&gt;The Ministerial Address by Stephen Morgan MP, UK Minister for Agriculture and Food.&lt;/figcaption&gt;
  
&lt;/figure&gt;

  
&lt;figure class=&quot;page-figure&quot;&gt;
  &lt;img
    src=&quot;/assets/img/events/2026-09-28-WATIS/maryna-kuzmenko-stephen-morgan-world-agri-tech-london-2026-1200.webp&quot;
    srcset=&quot;/assets/img/events/2026-09-28-WATIS/maryna-kuzmenko-stephen-morgan-world-agri-tech-london-2026-480.webp 480w, /assets/img/events/2026-09-28-WATIS/maryna-kuzmenko-stephen-morgan-world-agri-tech-london-2026-1200.webp 1200w&quot;
    sizes=&quot;(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 410px&quot;
    width=&quot;1200&quot;
    height=&quot;900&quot;
    alt=&quot;Dr. Maryna Kuzmenko in a selfie with Stephen Morgan MP, who is wearing a dark suit and tie, in a wood-panelled conference foyer.&quot;
    loading=&quot;lazy&quot;
    decoding=&quot;async&quot;&gt;
  
  
  
  &lt;figcaption&gt;Dr. Maryna Kuzmenko with Stephen Morgan MP, UK Minister for Agriculture and Food, at World Agri-Tech London 2026.&lt;/figcaption&gt;
  
&lt;/figure&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;num&quot;&gt;2.&lt;/span&gt; &quot;Does it work?&quot; has become &quot;How much does it cost?&quot;&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;One person told me that the biostimulant market is really crowded, and the practical question has moved on:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol class=&quot;post-steps&quot;&gt;
  &lt;li&gt;&quot;Does it work?&quot;&lt;/li&gt;
  &lt;li&gt;has become &quot;How much does it cost?&quot;&lt;/li&gt;
  &lt;li&gt;and &quot;How do we win the buyer&#39;s trust?&quot;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;So the startups that break through run independent, multi-season trials, and then keep working with those who bought, to measure their success and sell further with real names of happy clients.&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;figure class=&quot;page-figure&quot;&gt;
  &lt;img
    src=&quot;/assets/img/events/2026-09-28-WATIS/maryna-kuzmenko-mark-jarman-agriterra-world-agri-tech-2026-1200.webp&quot;
    srcset=&quot;/assets/img/events/2026-09-28-WATIS/maryna-kuzmenko-mark-jarman-agriterra-world-agri-tech-2026-480.webp 480w, /assets/img/events/2026-09-28-WATIS/maryna-kuzmenko-mark-jarman-agriterra-world-agri-tech-2026-1200.webp 1200w&quot;
    sizes=&quot;(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 860px&quot;
    width=&quot;1200&quot;
    height=&quot;675&quot;
    alt=&quot;Dr. Maryna Kuzmenko and Mark Jarman, in glasses and a light jacket, in a selfie in the conference foyer with delegates in the background.&quot;
    loading=&quot;lazy&quot;
    decoding=&quot;async&quot;&gt;
  
  
  
  &lt;figcaption&gt;Dr. Maryna Kuzmenko with Mark Jarman from AgriTERRA.&lt;/figcaption&gt;
  
&lt;/figure&gt;


&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;num&quot;&gt;3.&lt;/span&gt; Input dependency is the real risk&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;So now the focus is less on maximising yield and more on:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
  &lt;li&gt;cutting fertiliser,&lt;/li&gt;
  &lt;li&gt;cutting pesticides, and&lt;/li&gt;
  &lt;li&gt;reducing irrigation dependency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I heard that a tonne of urea now costs around 2.5 tonnes of wheat, up from 1.2 before the war in Ukraine.&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;figure class=&quot;page-figure&quot;&gt;
  &lt;img
    src=&quot;/assets/img/events/2026-09-28-WATIS/maryna-kuzmenko-mario-caccamo-kaust-world-agri-tech-2026-1200.webp&quot;
    srcset=&quot;/assets/img/events/2026-09-28-WATIS/maryna-kuzmenko-mario-caccamo-kaust-world-agri-tech-2026-480.webp 480w, /assets/img/events/2026-09-28-WATIS/maryna-kuzmenko-mario-caccamo-kaust-world-agri-tech-2026-1200.webp 1200w&quot;
    sizes=&quot;(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 860px&quot;
    width=&quot;1200&quot;
    height=&quot;900&quot;
    alt=&quot;Dr. Maryna Kuzmenko in a selfie with Professor Mario Caccamo, in a dark jacket and open shirt, in front of a marble wall in the conference foyer.&quot;
    loading=&quot;lazy&quot;
    decoding=&quot;async&quot;&gt;
  
  
  
  &lt;figcaption&gt;Dr. Maryna Kuzmenko with Professor Mario Caccamo from KAUST, the King Abdullah University of Science and Technology.&lt;/figcaption&gt;
  
&lt;/figure&gt;


&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;num&quot;&gt;4.&lt;/span&gt; Pitch before the budgets close&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I also noted down for myself (perhaps you are also curious 😉) a tip from Lely on how startups can succeed with global corporations: pitch before budgets are closed in October.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is a real insight, I believe. Only two days left, though :)&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;figure class=&quot;page-figure&quot;&gt;
  &lt;img
    src=&quot;/assets/img/events/2026-09-28-WATIS/maryna-kuzmenko-ming-fung-chua-elevate-dairy-world-agri-tech-2026-1200.webp&quot;
    srcset=&quot;/assets/img/events/2026-09-28-WATIS/maryna-kuzmenko-ming-fung-chua-elevate-dairy-world-agri-tech-2026-480.webp 480w, /assets/img/events/2026-09-28-WATIS/maryna-kuzmenko-ming-fung-chua-elevate-dairy-world-agri-tech-2026-1200.webp 1200w&quot;
    sizes=&quot;(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 860px&quot;
    width=&quot;1200&quot;
    height=&quot;900&quot;
    alt=&quot;Dr. Maryna Kuzmenko and Ming Fung Chua, both with green summit lanyards, smiling in a selfie in the conference foyer.&quot;
    loading=&quot;lazy&quot;
    decoding=&quot;async&quot;&gt;
  
  
  
  &lt;figcaption&gt;Dr. Maryna Kuzmenko with Ming Fung Chua from Elevate Dairy, Australia&amp;#39;s first dairy-focused landing pad, by the Gardiner Foundation.&lt;/figcaption&gt;
  
&lt;/figure&gt;


&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;num&quot;&gt;5.&lt;/span&gt; Resilience now means working offline&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;With natural disasters and wars, resilience now means working offline. In Ukraine, farm tools must run without GPS or internet, and mapping mines on fields is a digital priority.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It also matters for rural areas where connectivity is poor (thanks, Starlink, but it&#39;s a pretty expensive magic wand that many farmers can&#39;t afford).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Food security = national security.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;


